      "writtenOn": "2023-05-01T21:27:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can someone here please explain why this series is necessary? Cable data is already being transmitted to the kernel and then through the mux agent / IOM.\n\nFrom https://issuetracker.google.com/266823500#comment21:\n\u003e That\u0027s correct,  it\u0027s with existing interface.\nWe have changes in connector class and mux agent driver to handle this.\nWe are in the process of verifying the end to end flow with all these changes and will upstream the code once queries are resolved.\n\nSo, what is being implemented here? EnterMode from host to DP 2.1 active cables should be optional (AFAIK according to 4.11 of DP Alt mode v2.1)\n\nCan Intel please provide a 1 page summary? We\u0027d asked for something along those lines in https://buganizer.corp.google.com/issues/266823500, but this wasn\u0027t brought up then.\n\nThanks!",
      "revId": "6400fdc99993fdea3dd110f1d00f73e59fdab51a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a595ba48_23298e9d",
