      "writtenOn": "2023-05-24T17:26:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "MTL will support DP2.1 with DP alternate mode only. We will use the existing host command to use the Cable VDO data and will delete the new host command.",
      "parentUuid": "054309a2_4d08ff11",
      "revId": "6400fdc99993fdea3dd110f1d00f73e59fdab51a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "175e23eb_1d601506",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 33
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1181774
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-25T00:31:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The point is, if we are using the kernel alternate mode driver for 1 alternate mode, we need to do it for all the alternate modes (and USB4), regardless of what  DP version the other modes support. We can\u0027t have the kernel (drivers/usb/typec/altmodes/displayport.c) only handle DP alternate mode, but have the others handled by the EC.\n\nFTR, we have the infrastructure in place to send and receive VDMs from the AP, so we *can* get the alt mode drivers to work, just that it needs testing, and additional support for Thunderbolt compatibility mode.",
      "parentUuid": "179b89c3_62f1d20c",
      "revId": "6400fdc99993fdea3dd110f1d00f73e59fdab51a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b6f6e20a_a864e9cf",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 33
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1241068
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-25T16:28:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since, we are implementing DP2.1 for only DP alt mode and to stay consistent with current implementation of cros_ec_typec driver where all the alternate mode and USB4 is handled by EC, we inclined to use new host command to get details for additional parameters. We can still use ec_response_usb_pd_control_v2 considering additional parameters(UHBR13.5, DPAM) are yet not needed for DP2.1 cable identification.\n\nAs you mentioned if we want to implement same for other alt mode and usb4 that requires overhaul of the cros_ec_typec driver and additional validation as well as more discussions. I am not sure if that would be good idea at this stage of the MTL program.  For now, we can implement cable VDO usage for DP2.1 only and create tasks to extend it for all the alternate mode and USB4. When implementation is done for all alt modes, we can intercept it for next program.",
      "parentUuid": "175e23eb_1d601506",
      "revId": "6400fdc99993fdea3dd110f1d00f73e59fdab51a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
